WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:03.980
<b>Rescue on the Front
Line of Love</b>

3
00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:08.230
If you do not wish
to be aboard this ship,

4
00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:11.470
there is but one path left for you.

5
00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:15.440
Hm. Death... So long.

6
00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:20.750
There's no way I can
possibly beat this guy!

7
00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:25.490
But I'm not gonna stay on
this ship, that's for sure.

8
00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:27.570
I have no regrets!

9
00:02:27.570 --> 00:02:30.700
Yes. I know what you're thinking.

10
00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:36.580
And by now I'm sure you realize you
won't be leaving this ark safely.

11
00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:41.300
That is... unless you're pinning
your hopes on those two rats,

12
00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:43.800
who've just snuck on board.

13
00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:59.810
Lemme off this crazy thing!

14
00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:01.180
Sanji, listen!

15
00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:04.100
If we go any higher, we won't
be able to get down!

16
00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:06.310
Not to mention the fact
that God is on board!

17
00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:07.900
Or had you forgotten?

18
00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:11.150
We're already here, stupid!

19
00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:12.630
So just deal with it!

20
00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:14.760
But what are we gonna do, Sanji?

21
00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:18.220
Look at the size of this thing!
I've seen smaller mountains!

22
00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:20.430
There could be hundreds
of guys on board!

23
00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:22.310
We can't fight them all!

24
00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:26.810
Besides. If God or those
Priests are here...

25
00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:29.280
Oh, just get over it already!

26
00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:32.610
You're the one who's always
prepared for this kinda stuff!

27
00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:34.610
You got all the cool equipment!

28
00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:38.410
Well, this? Not what I had
in mind when I made 'em!

29
00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:43.100
Ugh. Well, the bad
guys've got that Mantra ability.

30
00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:44.450
They can predict our moves!

31
00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:46.610
No point in trying to be sneaky!

32
00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:50.400
In fact, I'd bet my favorite carving
knife they already know we're here!

33
00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:54.050
They know we're here?
So what are we supposed to do?

34
00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:56.630
Stop freakin' out for starters.

35
00:03:56.630 --> 00:04:00.340
Once we're safely inside, we'll
split up and head for the main deck.

36
00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.200
Nami's got to be up there.

37
00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:05.470
Hold on! Did you say split up?

38
00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:08.430
Are you out of your mind?!
Why would we do that?

39
00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:11.220
We have no idea how many
bad guys are on board!

40
00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:13.640
Just getting up here was
dangerous enough!

41
00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:15.030
You dumbass!

42
00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:19.820
If we don't split up,
we could both die.

43
00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:21.790
Both die?

44
00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:24.420
I don't suppose you'd
care to elaborate.

45
00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:27.650
Wait a minute. You're not gonna...

46
00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:31.530
You mean, to save Nami...

47
00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:34.790
Usopp. Listen to me.

48
00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:38.080
If it'll save Nami, I'll
gladly sacrifice your life.

49
00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:40.290
You jerk, why I oughta...!

50
00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:42.880
All right then! I'm coming, Nami!

51
00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:44.810
I'm not done yellin' at you!

52
00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:47.060
Hold on, Nami-swan!

53
00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:52.320
Wait, Sanji!
Hold on! Please! Buddy! Pal!

54
00:04:57.190 --> 00:05:00.200
It seems they're quite
serious about your rescue.

55
00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:03.020
Fools to the bitter end.

56
00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:05.120
Who can it be?

57
00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:08.070
No one besides Luffy can still move.

58
00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:11.030
Besides, how could they even
get on board the ark?

59
00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:28.510
Though help may have arrived,
it doesn't mean you've been saved yet.

60
00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:31.690
Nor am I obligated to wait for them.

61
00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:36.110
All I can do is jump overboard
and hope for the best.

62
00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:38.990
If I stay here, I'm dead for sure.

63
00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:43.210
I'm up against lightning.
What else can I do?

64
00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:58.000
What's all this?

65
00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:13.110
There's no one here!
But this ship is huge!

66
00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:15.860
Does it run without
anyone operating it?

67
00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:17.950
And how does it fly, anyway?

68
00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:20.740
I've never heard of
a flying ship before!

69
00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:22.640
Just the thought of being
up in the air like this

70
00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:26.150
makes my knees all wobbly! I feel sick!

71
00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:28.440
I wonder what the power
source for this thing is?

72
00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:32.440
Oh, what do I care, as long as
it doesn't decide to fall!

73
00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:34.030
Wait! I just realized!

74
00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:37.700
Even if Nami is on the upper deck,
we're way too high up now to jump off!

75
00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:39.790
What the hell are we gonna do?

76
00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:07.860
The sky. It keeps getting darker.

77
00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.820
And take it up with him.

78
00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:20.960
Onto the boats! Don't get left behind!

79
00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:23.380
Hurry to the White Sea!

80
00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:25.380
We're running out of time!

81
00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:29.510
Look at it. It's terrifying!

82
00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:32.380
This is really it!
The end of the world!

83
00:07:33.910 --> 00:07:37.120
Leave the village? But Chief.

84
00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:38.470
What about the warriors?

85
00:07:38.730 --> 00:07:40.520
They're still not back from Upper Yard!

86
00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:43.750
There is no need to wait.

87
00:07:45.890 --> 00:07:46.930
But Chief...

88
00:07:46.930 --> 00:07:48.860
We have no choice.

89
00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:54.280
The warriors aren't children,
they can avoid the dangers they face.

90
00:07:54.580 --> 00:07:56.210
Have faith in them.

91
00:07:58.310 --> 00:08:03.010
Eneru will destroy everything.
We know that.

92
00:08:03.010 --> 00:08:06.090
Just as he did to his homeland, Birka.

93
00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:11.680
So too shall he do here.
We must escape.

94
00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:14.780
Now. We must prepare the ships!

95
00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:18.490
Our first task is to save the
lives of the villagers here!

96
00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:30.120
Everything is coming to an end.

97
00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:32.960
Wyper. Let it go.

98
00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:35.460
You've done everything you could.

99
00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:40.670
Did you come from the Blue Sea World?

100
00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:42.090
If that's what you call it.

101
00:08:42.090 --> 00:08:44.430
We sailed up a river
of clouds to get here.

102
00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:47.310
Speaking of "here",
is this is your home?

103
00:08:47.310 --> 00:08:50.610
Everything is happening in this
forest right in front of me.

104
00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:52.810
And I have no way to
know what's going on!

105
00:08:55.150 --> 00:08:58.190
All I can do is wait!

106
00:08:58.190 --> 00:08:59.950
Suu?

107
00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:03.620
Everyone. I hope you're all safe!

108
00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:17.250
Horsey-Bird! Horsey-Bird!

109
00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:20.460
I'm sorry! You were
trying to protect me!

110
00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:27.210
Aisa! Aisa!

111
00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:28.640
Aisa!

112
00:09:28.640 --> 00:09:29.910
Luffy? Are you alive?

113
00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:36.040
Over here! This way! Aisa!

114
00:09:36.040 --> 00:09:38.840
– Aisa!

115
00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:40.440
Hey! Help me out!

116
00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:42.900
How did you land like that?

117
00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:54.150
All right. Dammit!

118
00:09:54.910 --> 00:09:56.900
I can't get this golden ball off!

119
00:09:56.900 --> 00:09:59.070
Hey, watch your mouth!

120
00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:02.320
Let's just get back to that
beanstalk where Robin was!

121
00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:04.580
I won't let Eneru get away with this!

122
00:10:04.630 --> 00:10:05.460
Okay!

123
00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:09.870
Nice try, jerk, but it takes
a lot more to stop me!

124
00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:13.500
Your ark's toast! And I know
just where to find you!

125
00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:36.370
Congratulations, young lady,
that was rather amusing!

126
00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:40.250
I did it.

127
00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:44.300
Such clever toys you
have down on the Blue Sea.

128
00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:49.130
Thunder Ball!

129
00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:58.290
Creating a path for
the lightning to follow.

130
00:10:58.290 --> 00:11:00.040
A clever tactic.

131
00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:04.260
You're obviously well-acquainted
with weather phenomena.

132
00:11:05.690 --> 00:11:08.020
But, it's not enough!

133
00:11:10.510 --> 00:11:13.040
You realize, of course, it's futile.

134
00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:17.870
All I need do is raise the voltage
and your trick won't work. Will it?

135
00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:23.550
Now, I'm a very busy man. Begone!

136
00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:27.180
Can't dodge this one!

137
00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:30.730
Why don't you begone? Exploding Star!

138
00:11:41.780 --> 00:11:43.950
Oops. I'm sorry.

139
00:11:44.810 --> 00:11:45.790
Usopp?

140
00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:49.170
I know you. From the ship.

141
00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:53.570
Hey! Where's Sanji?

142
00:11:53.570 --> 00:11:56.030
Sanji? He's here too?

143
00:11:56.030 --> 00:11:58.160
You mean he's not up here yet?!

144
00:11:58.160 --> 00:11:59.740
Wha...?

145
00:12:04.330 --> 00:12:05.870
I see...

146
00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:07.080
Later!

147
00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:08.710
Pansy!

148
00:12:16.680 --> 00:12:21.060
Be a man, Usopp.
What are you running for?

149
00:12:21.060 --> 00:12:23.270
Bring it on, God!

150
00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:31.400
Usopp!

151
00:12:34.530 --> 00:12:35.320
Nami!

152
00:12:35.610 --> 00:12:38.450
Yeah, what? Tell me
what to do, I'm on it!

153
00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:39.410
Please save me.

154
00:12:39.410 --> 00:12:40.910
Like hell!

155
00:12:40.910 --> 00:12:43.700
I thought you came here to
save me, you spineless chicken!

156
00:12:43.870 --> 00:12:47.200
Yeah, um. I'm not really sure
what's going on anymore.

157
00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:49.250
Then what are you doing here?

158
00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:49.980
Well...

159
00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:51.900
Well, what? Get your rear in
gear and save me, right now!

160
00:12:54.300 --> 00:12:57.680
How do I do that exactly?
We are fighting God.

161
00:12:57.680 --> 00:12:58.510
Oh, yeah!

162
00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:09.350
By the way, Nami, about that hat.

163
00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:11.100
Yeah, it's Luffy's.

164
00:13:11.250 --> 00:13:14.670
He was here a little while ago,
but Eneru threw him overboard!

165
00:13:14.670 --> 00:13:17.260
But he's not dead, I'm sure of it.

166
00:13:17.260 --> 00:13:18.630
The ark's gaining altitude!

167
00:13:18.630 --> 00:13:20.470
We can't count on Luffy to save us!

168
00:13:20.470 --> 00:13:21.510
Right.

169
00:13:21.510 --> 00:13:25.050
We gotta do this ourselves,
'cause I'm not a fan of dying!

170
00:13:25.050 --> 00:13:26.840
I'm with you there!

171
00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:29.160
Huh?

172
00:13:34.390 --> 00:13:36.670
Here. Come hide behind
this tube thingy!

173
00:13:36.670 --> 00:13:38.710
I'm bettin' it's pretty important.

174
00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:40.840
So he might not use his big attacks!

175
00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:43.880
Usopp! Look over there!

176
00:13:43.880 --> 00:13:46.280
Huh? Ah! A Waver!

177
00:13:46.280 --> 00:13:48.660
We'll have to jump off on that!

178
00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:50.990
Jump from this height?! Are you nuts?

179
00:13:50.990 --> 00:13:52.540
No, look!

180
00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:55.250
There's a patch of Island Cloud
in the middle of the forest!

181
00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:58.210
If we can reach that,
we just might make it!

182
00:13:58.210 --> 00:13:59.790
Of course!

183
00:14:03.210 --> 00:14:04.420
Dammit!

184
00:14:15.090 --> 00:14:18.340
I'll go try to create
a diversion! Get it ready!

185
00:14:18.340 --> 00:14:19.220
Right!

186
00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:21.380
Take this, God!

187
00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:24.590
Behold! Usopp Spell!

188
00:14:26.430 --> 00:14:30.520
A splinter embeds itself
deep under your fingernail!

189
00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:33.940
Ugh! That hurts just thinking about it!

190
00:14:33.940 --> 00:14:37.320
Cover your ears, you
idiot, this stuff can kill you!

191
00:14:38.700 --> 00:14:42.000
A piece of paper... cuts across
the skin of your knuckles!

192
00:14:45.530 --> 00:14:49.490
Five canker sores! Inflaming your gums!

193
00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:55.210
Usopp, no!

194
00:14:58.720 --> 00:15:00.430
Gotta get this thing running.

195
00:15:00.430 --> 00:15:03.020
We're only gonna get
one chance to escape!

196
00:15:06.290 --> 00:15:07.750
Hang on...

197
00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:16.520
Looks good.

198
00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:18.480
The Island Cloud is directly
below that beanstalk!

199
00:15:18.970 --> 00:15:20.590
I'm ready, let's get...

200
00:15:32.220 --> 00:15:35.520
Though you may
desperately want to run away...

201
00:15:35.520 --> 00:15:38.810
...facing me, it will
not be that simple.

202
00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:43.570
But please, do try it again.

203
00:15:43.570 --> 00:15:47.400
I always enjoy a deadly game of tag.

204
00:15:58.690 --> 00:16:00.310
Usopp, grab my hand!

205
00:16:02.170 --> 00:16:03.630
Come on!

206
00:16:15.060 --> 00:16:18.480
For you, there is no hope of salvation.

207
00:16:32.370 --> 00:16:33.950
Get going.

208
00:16:33.950 --> 00:16:34.660
El...

209
00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:36.120
Sanji, run!

210
00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:37.810
Gun it, Nami!

211
00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:41.730
...Thor!

212
00:16:47.840 --> 00:16:50.220
Usopp, wait! Let off the gas!

213
00:16:50.220 --> 00:16:51.390
What about Sanji?

214
00:16:51.390 --> 00:16:53.600
Don't stop! We've gotta escape!

215
00:16:53.600 --> 00:16:57.520
Now stop making my plan
sound bad! And keep going!

216
00:17:08.850 --> 00:17:12.940
So they jumped.

217
00:17:12.940 --> 00:17:16.490
Do they still not understand
the range of my powers?

218
00:17:16.560 --> 00:17:19.350
They haven't escaped me
in the slightest.

219
00:17:20.080 --> 00:17:21.370
Hm?

220
00:17:24.940 --> 00:17:26.820
Hey, God.

221
00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:29.700
There's something I wanted to tell you.

222
00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:32.700
Oh... But first...

223
00:17:34.190 --> 00:17:37.030
...I... should thank you.

224
00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:45.750
I was looking...
for a light. 'preciate it.

225
00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:50.570
Right. Do you have a point?

226
00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:56.120
Yeah, get ready to cry, bastard.

227
00:18:07.250 --> 00:18:08.460
Hm.

228
00:18:09.930 --> 00:18:11.180
Hm?

229
00:18:30.440 --> 00:18:34.400
Get ready to cry, bastard.

230
00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:36.640
Damn you!

231
00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:40.340
You did something below deck!

232
00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:42.510
What have you done to my ark?!

233
00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:47.310
You fool!

234
00:18:47.600 --> 00:18:48.970
You wretched fool!

235
00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:53.150
The gears have gone awry.

236
00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:54.320
I must fix them.

237
00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:19.100
Don't you worry.

238
00:19:19.100 --> 00:19:21.390
Nami fell safely into
some island clouds.

239
00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:37.870
No!

240
00:19:37.870 --> 00:19:39.750
Oh, no! We're gonna crash!

241
00:19:39.750 --> 00:19:41.550
We're gonna crash
and then we're gonna die!

242
00:19:55.800 --> 00:19:57.760
Usopp! Sanji!

243
00:19:58.340 --> 00:19:59.930
Nami, is that you?

244
00:19:59.930 --> 00:20:01.560
Sounds like you
made it down, all right.

245
00:20:01.560 --> 00:20:02.890
What a relief!

246
00:20:02.870 --> 00:20:04.120
Sanji!

247
00:20:04.060 --> 00:20:05.810
Sanji, are you okay?

248
00:20:05.460 --> 00:20:07.380
Oh, you got burnt to a crisp for us.

249
00:20:07.380 --> 00:20:11.710
I'm so sorry! I promise I'll
make it up to you somehow!

250
00:20:11.710 --> 00:20:14.090
I can't breathe! I can't breathe!

251
00:20:14.090 --> 00:20:17.220
Nami, hurry! Hurry up and
pull me out! I can't breathe!

252
00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:19.850
Oh, sorry. All right.

253
00:20:19.850 --> 00:20:21.970
Let's get the heck outta here!

254
00:20:43.390 --> 00:20:46.980
This vessel is not
so easily brought down.

255
00:20:47.360 --> 00:20:50.610
I am fully acquainted
with the ark's drive circuits.

256
00:20:53.240 --> 00:20:55.990
We may lack electricity,
but a backup system

257
00:20:55.990 --> 00:21:01.370
harnesses the wind power of 200 Jet
Dials I gathered in my homeland of Birka.

258
00:21:03.910 --> 00:21:07.910
They will keep this ship
aloft for quite some time.

259
00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:12.000
No matter what you feeble beings try...

260
00:21:22.920 --> 00:21:27.380
This land and all its pathetic
inhabitants will perish.

261
00:21:30.210 --> 00:21:32.550
'Kay guys, check out that huge vine.

262
00:21:33.060 --> 00:21:35.690
If it's the same one I saw
when I was down in the ruins,

263
00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:39.190
then it stands to reason we're on
the Island Clouds right above them.

264
00:21:39.260 --> 00:21:41.550
Ruins? Oh, The City of Gold!

265
00:21:41.550 --> 00:21:42.680
It's real?

266
00:21:42.680 --> 00:21:44.180
It's real.

267
00:21:44.180 --> 00:21:47.000
But Eneru took all the gold
that was there for himself.

268
00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:49.160
If the ruins are beneath us,
Zoro and the others

269
00:21:47.740 --> 00:21:51.580
<b>Ruins of Shandora</b>

270
00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:51.580
<b>Current Location</b>

271
00:21:49.900 --> 00:21:51.110
should be down there.

272
00:21:52.330 --> 00:21:54.460
I may not know the lay of the land...

273
00:21:55.870 --> 00:21:58.920
But I do know one thing:
staying here is dangerous.

274
00:22:01.040 --> 00:22:02.460
You got that right.

275
00:22:02.630 --> 00:22:04.850
Hop on! Let's find everyone
and get off this island.

276
00:22:05.380 --> 00:22:06.590
That's a plan!

277
00:22:08.140 --> 00:22:12.310
There are no safe
places left in Skypiea.

278
00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:31.710
Luffy! Look out!

279
00:22:32.040 --> 00:22:34.630
Huh?

280
00:22:39.380 --> 00:22:41.340
So fast!

281
00:22:41.340 --> 00:22:43.220
No, wait! Luffy!

282
00:22:43.220 --> 00:22:46.260
That's the wrong way! Go left! Left!

283
00:22:47.390 --> 00:22:50.850
There's no way I can turn that sharp!

284
00:22:50.850 --> 00:22:52.850
Gum-Gum...

285
00:22:52.850 --> 00:22:53.980
...Hook!

286
00:23:02.030 --> 00:23:04.820
Stop destroying my homeland!

287
00:23:05.410 --> 00:23:07.620
Giant Jack is over that-a-way!

288
00:23:08.070 --> 00:23:09.330
I know, but...

289
00:23:18.350 --> 00:23:19.150
Oh, man.

290
00:23:19.150 --> 00:23:20.940
Robin and the others are gone.

291
00:23:22.260 --> 00:23:23.970
Zoro and Chopper.

292
00:23:26.220 --> 00:23:29.520
I'm guessing they
must have climbed up already.

293
00:23:29.520 --> 00:23:31.600
Yeah, Robin must have helped them.

294
00:23:31.600 --> 00:23:32.690
Let's go.

295
00:23:35.570 --> 00:23:36.730
Hey, Aisa.

296
00:23:42.860 --> 00:23:46.950
Will the sky islands
really be destroyed?

297
00:24:07.590 --> 00:24:08.960
Wyper and the others.

298
00:24:08.960 --> 00:24:10.420
They're right through here!

299
00:24:17.980 --> 00:24:20.860
I suspect the ship is
moving toward the Grand Belfry.

300
00:24:21.610 --> 00:24:24.230
Wonder what happened to
Miss Navigator and the boys.

301
00:24:24.230 --> 00:24:27.320
If they're on that ship,
it could mean they're...

302
00:24:31.280 --> 00:24:32.700
We're through!

303
00:24:38.160 --> 00:24:39.580
Luffy, down there!

304
00:24:39.580 --> 00:24:41.880
Stop! Stop!

305
00:24:41.880 --> 00:24:43.110
Robin!

306
00:24:43.420 --> 00:24:45.210
What're you doing?

307
00:24:45.210 --> 00:24:46.840
Look after these two for me!

308
00:24:57.790 --> 00:24:59.530
Whoa-whoa-whoa-whoa-whoa!

309
00:24:59.530 --> 00:25:00.530
Stop!

310
00:25:02.230 --> 00:25:03.520
Luffy!

311
00:25:04.780 --> 00:25:07.030
You grew extra hands!

312
00:25:07.030 --> 00:25:09.370
What have you got on your arm?

313
00:25:09.370 --> 00:25:10.750
Robin!

314
00:25:10.750 --> 00:25:13.760
The golden bell is at the
top of this vine, right?

315
00:25:13.760 --> 00:25:16.920
And Eneru is trying to get
his hands on it, isn't he?

316
00:25:16.920 --> 00:25:18.460
That's right.

317
00:25:18.460 --> 00:25:22.470
If the Grand Belfry exists,
then the bell would be there.

318
00:25:21.960 --> 00:25:22.830
But he's already...

319
00:25:23.470 --> 00:25:24.470
Good.

320
00:25:26.460 --> 00:25:27.420
Luffy!

321
00:25:28.570 --> 00:25:29.900
So, young lady.

322
00:25:30.570 --> 00:25:32.360
Have you seen our navigator?

323
00:25:32.360 --> 00:25:33.780
A woman with orange hair?

324
00:25:34.010 --> 00:25:35.850
You mean Nami? She's on the ship.

325
00:25:38.060 --> 00:25:38.760
Huh...

326
00:25:38.760 --> 00:25:41.100
I only hear one voice
coming from the sky.

327
00:25:47.400 --> 00:25:48.610
There they are!

328
00:25:52.740 --> 00:25:54.280
Whoa! Robin!

329
00:25:54.530 --> 00:25:56.410
Miss Navigator. With Long Nose.

330
00:25:56.410 --> 00:25:57.500
And the Cook too.

331
00:25:59.700 --> 00:26:01.000
Aisa!

332
00:26:01.790 --> 00:26:03.830
Thank goodness! You all right?

333
00:26:03.830 --> 00:26:05.590
Nami!

334
00:26:05.930 --> 00:26:06.890
Huh?

335
00:26:07.170 --> 00:26:08.920
Zoro! Chopper!

336
00:26:08.920 --> 00:26:10.550
Weird Old Guy!

337
00:26:10.550 --> 00:26:12.630
And a guerilla!

338
00:26:12.640 --> 00:26:16.290
Oh, oh, oh! Everyone's been taken down!

339
00:26:16.290 --> 00:26:18.710
Oh! If only I had been here!

340
00:26:18.710 --> 00:26:20.170
Wait, Aisa, where's Luffy?

341
00:26:20.170 --> 00:26:21.630
Wasn't he with you?

342
00:26:21.630 --> 00:26:24.510
Luffy climbed up
the vine to rescue you.

343
00:26:24.510 --> 00:26:26.800
But since everyone's here,
Luffy has to face Eneru

344
00:26:27.060 --> 00:26:29.230
by himself!

345
00:26:29.230 --> 00:26:31.060
We missed him, didn't we?

346
00:26:31.060 --> 00:26:32.270
Just now.

347
00:26:32.270 --> 00:26:34.690
I tried to stop him,
but he wouldn't listen.

348
00:26:34.690 --> 00:26:36.570
Dammit, Luffy.

349
00:26:36.570 --> 00:26:38.540
He knows we're running short on time.

350
00:26:38.620 --> 00:26:39.990
We gotta go now!

351
00:26:40.870 --> 00:26:44.750
Go on without me. I'll take
the waver and find him.

352
00:26:44.750 --> 00:26:46.760
Just try to get to the Merry somehow!

353
00:26:51.590 --> 00:26:53.590
Ah, man!

354
00:26:53.590 --> 00:26:56.680
That ship is movin' fast!

355
00:26:56.680 --> 00:26:59.890
Eneru!

356
00:27:00.640 --> 00:27:06.400
<b>Shandian Village
Hidden in the Clouds</b>

357
00:27:02.260 --> 00:27:03.850
Quickly! Get on the ships!

358
00:27:03.850 --> 00:27:05.930
The whole sky is turning black!

359
00:27:12.320 --> 00:27:13.490
What's wrong?

360
00:27:13.490 --> 00:27:15.240
We need to flee at once.

361
00:27:15.530 --> 00:27:17.910
My daughter Aisa. She still hasn't...

362
00:27:17.910 --> 00:27:20.950
Ah. She still hasn't returned.

363
00:27:20.950 --> 00:27:23.250
Aisa is a bright child.

364
00:27:23.250 --> 00:27:27.280
We must have faith that she is with
some warriors and will be protected.

365
00:27:31.030 --> 00:27:34.830
Hmph. The thunderclouds
are gushing out nicely now.

366
00:27:38.220 --> 00:27:43.850
<b>Angel Island
Skypiea</b>

367
00:27:44.310 --> 00:27:46.520
Hurry! Hurry up!

368
00:27:46.890 --> 00:27:51.100
Captain! If we don't use the boats at
the dock, we'll never fit everyone in!

369
00:27:51.100 --> 00:27:53.230
They'd have to sail all the way around!

370
00:27:53.230 --> 00:27:54.650
You men!

371
00:27:54.650 --> 00:27:56.980
Use dials to create rivers
inside the island at once!

372
00:27:58.460 --> 00:28:00.300
How many of the islanders are left?

373
00:28:00.300 --> 00:28:02.180
Almost half of them!

374
00:28:02.180 --> 00:28:04.510
People only, no more baggage!

375
00:28:04.510 --> 00:28:07.510
And get everybody
out to sea right away!

376
00:28:07.750 --> 00:28:08.920
Yes, sir!

377
00:28:17.590 --> 00:28:18.590
Hold it!

378
00:28:18.710 --> 00:28:23.340
Nobody's leaving until everyone pays
the 2 billion Extol departure fee!

379
00:28:23.340 --> 00:28:24.460
Amazon, hurry!

380
00:28:24.460 --> 00:28:26.600
You can still escape with us!

381
00:28:26.600 --> 00:28:27.480
Huh?

382
00:28:27.060 --> 00:28:31.980
<b>Heaven's Gate
White Sea</b>

383
00:28:27.480 --> 00:28:29.310
Hurry to Cloud End!

384
00:28:29.310 --> 00:28:30.230
Huh?

385
00:28:30.230 --> 00:28:34.530
The sky islands...
are about to be destroyed!

386
00:28:36.740 --> 00:28:38.700
Oh, my.

387
00:28:55.050 --> 00:28:56.760
The wind has stopped.

388
00:29:19.070 --> 00:29:21.240
Run! Run!

389
00:29:31.760 --> 00:29:32.850
Now, then.

390
00:29:34.520 --> 00:29:36.810
Let us begin the festivities.

391
00:29:38.980 --> 00:29:40.900
The time for endings has come.

392
00:29:48.930 --> 00:29:50.640
Mamaragan.

393
00:30:00.450 --> 00:30:03.360
<b>Angel Island
White-White Sea</b>

394
00:30:00.860 --> 00:30:02.660
Get away from the island!

395
00:30:02.920 --> 00:30:05.550
Run! Don't look back!

396
00:30:05.950 --> 00:30:08.410
The lightning keeps getting bigger!

397
00:30:08.510 --> 00:30:10.800
The boats at the
docks have been destroyed!

398
00:30:10.800 --> 00:30:12.680
To the western end of the beach!

399
00:30:13.290 --> 00:30:14.750
Quickly! There are still boats there!

400
00:30:14.750 --> 00:30:16.130
Run to the west!

401
00:30:16.430 --> 00:30:17.770
Move, people!

402
00:30:17.770 --> 00:30:19.350
Leave your belongings!

403
00:30:29.220 --> 00:30:30.100
Chief!

404
00:30:30.100 --> 00:30:31.390
We need to get you on a boat!

405
00:30:33.600 --> 00:30:36.400
Great warrior Kalgara.

406
00:30:37.820 --> 00:30:39.440
I beg you.

407
00:30:39.440 --> 00:30:40.860
Protect us all.

408
00:30:56.310 --> 00:30:58.640
Man, those lightning bolts are huge!

409
00:30:59.090 --> 00:31:02.170
We're gonna end up
sky dust if we stay here!

410
00:31:04.820 --> 00:31:06.570
Guys! Go now!

411
00:31:06.570 --> 00:31:09.150
Once I find Luffy,
we'll be right behind you!

412
00:31:09.150 --> 00:31:11.030
Uh, yeah, right! I gotcha!

413
00:31:17.560 --> 00:31:18.770
Hurry, Robin!

414
00:31:19.400 --> 00:31:22.030
We gotta find a way to
carry these guys to the ship!

415
00:31:22.030 --> 00:31:23.240
Wyper!

416
00:31:31.620 --> 00:31:32.790
Swordsman!

417
00:31:34.370 --> 00:31:35.460
Weird Old Guy!

418
00:31:35.710 --> 00:31:37.470
Oh, good, you're awake now!

419
00:31:37.470 --> 00:31:38.800
There's not a moment to lose!

420
00:31:38.800 --> 00:31:40.800
D'you think you can walk yet?

421
00:31:40.800 --> 00:31:43.640
So... Eneru has begun.

422
00:31:49.860 --> 00:31:51.450
We must all hurry now.

423
00:31:52.010 --> 00:31:54.600
There is truly nothing
more we can do here.

424
00:31:58.560 --> 00:32:00.060
Wyper.

425
00:32:04.160 --> 00:32:05.700
We have to get out of here!

426
00:32:05.700 --> 00:32:08.660
Not even Luffy can handle
an enemy who can fly!

427
00:32:08.660 --> 00:32:11.580
I have to get to him before
this island is obliterated!

428
00:32:22.180 --> 00:32:23.590
Magnificent!

429
00:32:25.600 --> 00:32:30.060
You better not think for a second that I'm
gonna let you get away with this, Eneru!

430
00:32:33.030 --> 00:32:38.550
When you're lost and alone, call out and lead me to your side

431
00:32:38.770 --> 00:32:43.970
As you wander far from home, you search the sky and never hide

432
00:32:43.970 --> 00:32:46.770
You are so much like the moon

433
00:32:46.770 --> 00:32:51.420
Calmer than a star, your twinkling's lost

434
00:32:54.870 --> 00:33:03.820
A deep reflection shines, you slowly leave, fading, and what's the cost?

435
00:33:03.880 --> 00:33:09.050
Stay as you are, don't lose your way

436
00:33:09.050 --> 00:33:17.360
Let my words guide you, and look ahead until the day!

437
00:33:18.000 --> 00:33:24.250
Don't give up on your dreams, through endless nights they come to you

438
00:33:24.250 --> 00:33:29.870
If you stop, you'll never see them shining through!

439
00:33:31.110 --> 00:33:35.640
Will you return? Maybe not... Will you learn? I hope you do

440
00:33:35.640 --> 00:33:42.030
Please put your past to rest, and live your life anew.
